###############################################################################
#  NAMED INDIVIDUAL DECLARATIONS AND owl:AllDifferent
#
#  Mirrors the pattern taught in Week 9, Example #2 (the four string
#  instruments declared owl:NamedIndividual and then owl:AllDifferent).
#
#  Why this matters here. OWL makes NO unique-name assumption: without an
#  explicit statement, a reasoner is free to conclude that two differently
#  named individuals are the same thing. That silently breaks every
#  cardinality inference. Measured on this dataset, :ProlificPhilosopher
#  (authored min 3 Work) classifies 1 member without the owl:AllDifferent
#  axiom below and 2 members with it. See REPORT.md Section 6.
###############################################################################

# --- TimePeriod (5) ---
:ClassicalGreece a owl:NamedIndividual .
:EarlyModernPeriod a owl:NamedIndividual .
:MedievalPeriod a owl:NamedIndividual .
:NineteenthCentury a owl:NamedIndividual .
:TwentiethCentury a owl:NamedIndividual .

# --- Country (3) ---
:France a owl:NamedIndividual . :Greece a owl:NamedIndividual .
:Prussia a owl:NamedIndividual .

# --- City (3) ---
:Athens a owl:NamedIndividual . :Konigsberg a owl:NamedIndividual .
:Paris a owl:NamedIndividual .

# --- SchoolOfThought (16) ---
:AnalyticPhilosophy a owl:NamedIndividual .
:AncientGreekPhilosophy a owl:NamedIndividual .
:ContinentalPhilosophy a owl:NamedIndividual .
:EarlyModernPhilosophy a owl:NamedIndividual .
:Empiricism a owl:NamedIndividual . :Existentialism a owl:NamedIndividual .
:GermanIdealism a owl:NamedIndividual .
